From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] distributed: all-reduce through pinned host memory for GPUs
 without peer access

Two GPUs without peer access (consumer cards on a board without P2P):
small all-reduces (decode) go through pinned host memory in NCCL's LL
form (SGLANG_LL_ALLREDUCE), large ones (prefill) are staged through
pinned host memory with the copy engines (SGLANG_HOST_STAGED_ALLREDUCE).
Off unless set; the public repo's launcher sets both for two GPUs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
